<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Decebalus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 106 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Decebalus was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacia">Dacia</a> from 87 to 106 CE. He destroyed the Roman army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornelius-fuscus">Cornelius Fuscus</a> and in 89 CE won a favourable peace from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domitian">Domitian</a>, with Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subsidy">subsidies</a> and engineers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a>'s two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajans-dacian-wars">Dacian Wars</a> of 101–102 and 105–106 CE destroyed his kingdom; when his capital Sarmizegetusa fell he killed himself rather than be captured, and Dacia became a Roman province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/decebalus.jpg" alt="Decebalus" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harpeam · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Decebal_suicide.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…the Iazyges, who settled between the Danube and the Tisza, destroyed a Roman legion in Domitian's Sarmatian war of 92 CE; the Roxolani joined <b>Decebalus</b> of Dacia against Trajan; and in the Marcomannic Wars the Iazyges fought Marcus Aurelius until their king Zanticus made peace in 175 CE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sarmatians">Sarmatians · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After Burebista's murder in 44 BCE the realm split, but it was again a strong kingdom under <b>Decebalus</b>, whose forces destroyed a Roman army under Cornelius Fuscus in 86 or 87 CE.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-dacia">Kingdom of Dacia</a></li></ul></section>
